concept", "title": "Proportionality"}], "description": "Students learn the main justifications for punishment and how each theory shapes correctional policy."}, {"id": "070fd5ba-32ea-40f3-be28-689c2cc15b4b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "History of American corrections", "children": [{"id": "e0a1c967-6753-4c56-970d-11959e8c2f35", "type": "concept", "title": "Colonial punishments"}, {"id": "e65431a5-0e9c-4181-89b2-52aff6190058", "type": "concept", "title": "Pennsylvania system"}, {"id": "671db859-8f72-4f48-89fa-f97ab5cf37ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Auburn system"}, {"id": "3ac6f512-ce57-4a3f-86a4-7dddc5ee20f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Penitentiary ideal"}, {"id": "5809f452-957a-4a1f-a9d6-c03d4d56d7a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Reformatory movement"}, {"id": "8ba8cc14-f77e-4a4e-ab6e-aeb9eda49415", "type": "concept", "title": "Progressive era"}, {"id": "80b75756-30a9-4d95-a5b9-1d1be2d09f86", "type": "concept", "title": "Medical model"}, {"id": "656ff1f9-8e7d-46de-8eba-de7ede7026f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Nothing works era"}, {"id": "9b40830c-2e8d-4f8c-adae-2e65a7742930", "type": "concept", "title": "Mass incarceration"}], "description": "The point is to see prisons, jails, probation, and parole as historically produced institutions, not natural or fixed arrangements."}, {"id": "a21b65ef-ffd9-4001-9cd8-fbc3a0f92d43", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Correctional system map", "children": [{"id": "72c6e6ef-88ea-4db7-a7bb-891b975be892", "type": "concept", "title": "Pretrial detention"}, {"id": "7c80c065-03a3-4e5c-b85f-33dfd32a06bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Jail"}, {"id": "fd944676-c52b-4f4f-a772-e7e09b8ab700", "type": "concept", "title": "Prison"}, {"id": "fbfc1071-32ae-4748-a808-299c686f9f27", "type": "concept", "title": "Probation"}, {"id": "a8e20147-eb2a-4816-8a86-ef24cd774df7", "type": "concept", "title": "Parole"}, {"id": "41de9e50-3a6f-43db-ba58-49eb0ae2dccd", "type": "concept", "title": "Community corrections"}, {"id": "7782b9eb-f662-40a8-9fe